Z||000000||LPR||04-30-2001||08:40 PM||||Back at it again...<BR>I have an 84, standard.  I replaced a bad engine in my car with a new one and the problem didn't go away! grrrrrr<P>The problem is that it loops at idle and when I depress the clutch while stopping the RPM drops right past idle and stalls.<P>This happens sometimes, makes no difference if its warm or not.  I have checked the vacuum lines and have replaced the TPS with no difference. OH, one other thing, you know that hose on the intake that goes to the exhaust for warm idle air... yea, I don't have that, I don't know were it went! Is it important??<P>------------------<BR>1984 SE 89K<BR>"Your only as smart as your weakest think."||||reg||9
Z||000001||HummelHund||04-30-2001||10:06 PM||||If it's the same prob with both cars, have you checked the ECM wiring? Did you use the same TBI off the old engine with the new one? I'm having the same problem with my '84 SE and I've been told it may be the IAC. Apparently if it's seized it can cause this sort of thing. Check out my thread about my problem for more info on that, it's called "Fixed one problem, now it's another!!!"<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
